th, td { border: 1px solid #9aa5b4; padding: 4pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 1</h1>
<p><strong>Name: ____________________   Date: __________   Score: ______ / 100</strong></p>
<p>Closed book. Answer in the voice of the agent handling the ticket. For each scenario, state <strong>how you handle it</strong> (route + action) and <strong>the one trap</strong> that would fail the ticket. <strong>Section A — 6 points each; Section B (multiple choice) — 2 points each. Total 100.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1.</strong> A customer writes: <em>"I got the email saying my order shipped 4 days ago, but UPS still just says 'Label Created' and it hasn't moved. Did it actually ship?"</em> How do you respond, and what must you <strong>not</strong> promise?</p>
<p><strong>Q2.</strong> <em>"I registered late and my son has a tournament this Saturday. Can you rush my order so it gets here in time?"</em> What is the correct response?</p>
<p><strong>Q3.</strong> <em>"My daughter wore her jersey twice — washed cold, hung dry — and the number is already peeling off."</em> What do you do before taking any action, and what size do you replace with?</p>
<p><strong>Q4.</strong> <em>"The shirt we got is too small. Can I just exchange it for the next size up?"</em> What is the correct handling, and what is the policy you must state?</p>
<p><strong>Q5.</strong> <em>"I accidentally placed this order twice. Please cancel one of them — I only need one."</em> Walk through what you check and do before confirming the cancellation.</p>
<p><strong>Q6.</strong> <em>"I don't want to buy the whole mandatory kit again — I just need to order a couple of extra socks for my son. How?"</em> Explain the exact steps you'd give the customer.</p>
<p><strong>Q7.</strong> <em>"I can't get into the Rush Maryland team store — what's the password?"</em> How do you handle this, and what must you never do?</p>
<p><strong>Q8.</strong> <em>"The jersey size I need is out of stock. When will it be back, and what are my options right now?"</em> What options can you offer, and what must you avoid promising?</p>
<p><strong>Q9.</strong> <em>"This is ridiculous. Give me a phone number for your manager — I'm going to leave a Trustpilot review."</em> How do you handle this escalation? What do you tell them about phone support?</p>
<p><strong>Q10. Spot the mistake.</strong> A teammate drafted this reply — identify <strong>every</strong> thing wrong with it:</p>
<blockquote><em>"Hi! No problem, we'll exchange your medium for a large and ship it today — it'll arrive by Friday guaranteed. I've created replacement RO#48213 for you. — Thanks!"</em></blockquote>
<p>List each error and give the corrected handling.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Section B — Multiple Choice (Q11–Q30)</h2>
<p>Choose the single best answer. 2 points each.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> A customer wants to exchange an unworn shirt for a larger size. Correct action?</p>
<ul><li>A) No exchanges — return for refund, then place a new order</li><li>B) Process a direct size exchange</li><li>C) Ship the larger size and bill the difference</li><li>D) Tell them the item is non-returnable</li></ul>
<p><strong>12.</strong> What is the standard return window for eligible items?</p>
<ul><li>A) 14 days</li><li>B) 90 days</li><li>C) 30 days</li><li>D) 60 days</li></ul>
<p><strong>13.</strong> Where do customers ship returns?</p>
<ul><li>A) The club's address</li><li>B) Capelli Sport Returns, 901 Sathers Drive, Pittston, PA 18640</li><li>C) The fulfillment center overseas</li><li>D) Any Capelli outlet store</li></ul>
<p><strong>14.</strong> On a customer's statement, a refund appears as:</p>
<ul><li>A) "CAPELLI SPORT"</li><li>B) "REFUND"</li><li>C) The club name</li><li>D) "TEAMS US"</li></ul>
<p><strong>15.</strong> Refund timing to quote for a BigCommerce cancellation:</p>
<ul><li>A) Same day</li><li>B) 24 hours</li><li>C) 30 days</li><li>D) 3–5 business days</li></ul>
<p><strong>16.</strong> "Label Created" with no movement for days usually means:</p>
<ul><li>A) The package is lost</li><li>B) The label prints before the parcel ships; UPS hasn't scanned it yet</li><li>C) The order was cancelled</li><li>D) The address was wrong</li></ul>
<p><strong>17.</strong> Before replacing a defective item, you must:</p>
<ul><li>A) Issue a refund first</li><li>B) Get the customer's card</li><li>C) Request a clear evidence photo</li><li>D) Close the ticket</li></ul>
<p><strong>18.</strong> A replacement for a defective item is sent in:</p>
<ul><li>A) The same size/form originally ordered</li><li>B) The next size up</li><li>C) Any size the customer prefers</li><li>D) A size chosen by the fulfillment center</li></ul>
<p><strong>19.</strong> Does Capelli offer expedited/rush shipping?</p>
<ul><li>A) Yes, for a fee</li><li>B) Yes, for tournaments</li><li>C) No</li><li>D) Only on Shopify</li></ul>
<p><strong>20.</strong> Personalized items (name/number) are:</p>
<ul><li>A) Always returnable</li><li>B) Returnable within 60 days</li><li>C) Exchangeable only</li><li>D) Non-returnable/exchangeable unless Capelli made an error</li></ul>
<p><strong>21.</strong> A customer asks for the team-store password. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Provide it</li><li>B) Direct them to their coach/club admin</li><li>C) Reset it for them</li><li>D) Email it after an ID check</li></ul>
<p><strong>22.</strong> Player numbers/roster are controlled by:</p>
<ul><li>A) Capelli CS</li><li>B) The fulfillment center</li><li>C) The club admin/coach</li><li>D) The customer at checkout</li></ul>
<p><strong>23.</strong> To order individual items, the customer must first:</p>
<ul><li>A) Call Capelli</li><li>B) Wait 24h after the mandatory kit, sign in (same email, PC/Mac), and use "Enable Adding Individual Products"</li><li>C) Create a new club</li><li>D) Email a manager</li></ul>
<p><strong>24.</strong> Can you add an item to an existing order?</p>
<ul><li>A) Yes</li><li>B) Yes, within 24h</li><li>C) Only socks</li><li>D) No — place a new order; courtesy shipping refund</li></ul>
<p><strong>25.</strong> Processing time for a mandatory team kit is about:</p>
<ul><li>A) 3–4 business days</li><li>B) 1 week</li><li>C) ~5 weeks</li><li>D) 24 hours</li></ul>
<p><strong>26.</strong> A customer ordered the wrong size themselves. This is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Capelli's fault → replacement</li><li>B) Customer fault → return for refund + new order</li><li>C) A defect</li><li>D) An exchange</li></ul>
<p><strong>27.</strong> Capelli shipped the wrong item. This is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Customer fault</li><li>B) Not covered</li><li>C) Capelli fault → evidence photo + ship the correct item</li><li>D) A return</li></ul>
<p><strong>28.</strong> Which must NEVER appear in a customer email?</p>
<ul><li>A) The tracking number</li><li>B) The order number</li><li>C) The return address</li><li>D) The internal RO number</li></ul>
<p><strong>29.</strong> A customer threatens a bad review and demands a manager's phone number. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Give the manager's cell</li><li>B) Explain phone support isn't offered (email only) and escalate the complaint</li><li>C) Offer a refund immediately</li><li>D) Close the ticket</li></ul>
<p><strong>30.</strong> A never-received order where the season is already over — you:</p>
<ul><li>A) Auto-reship</li><li>B) Send another holding reply</li><li>C) Escalate for a refund/credit decision</li><li>D) Tell them to wait</li></ul></body></html>